    <specificationRepository>
      <specificationSpec>
        <specificationIdent specificationIdentNumber="HMI-SYM-001"/>
        <specificationTitle>Standard Display Symbols</specificationTitle>
        <specificationContent>
          <para>Standard symbology shall be used across all display types to ensure crew familiarity and reduce interpretation errors.</para>
          <table>
            <tgroup cols="3">
              <thead>
                <row>
                  <entry>Symbol</entry>
                  <entry>Description</entry>
                  <entry>Usage</entry>
                </row>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry>⚠ (Triangle with exclamation)</entry>
                  <entry>Warning Symbol</entry>
                  <entry>Precedes all warning-level messages and caution-level alerts</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>✓ (Check mark)</entry>
                  <entry>Normal/Complete Status</entry>
                  <entry>Indicates system is operating normally or task is complete</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>✗ (X mark)</entry>
                  <entry>Failed/Unavailable</entry>
                  <entry>Indicates system failure or data unavailable</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>⬆ ⬇ ⬅ ➡</entry>
                  <entry>Directional Arrows</entry>
                  <entry>Indicate trend, required action direction, or data flow</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>⊕ (Circle with plus)</entry>
                  <entry>Selected/Active</entry>
                  <entry>Indicates crew-selected item or active autopilot mode</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>⊗ (Circle with X)</entry>
                  <entry>Inhibited/Disabled</entry>
                  <entry>Indicates system intentionally disabled or function inhibited</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>◆ (Diamond)</entry>
                  <entry>Advisory Information</entry>
                  <entry>Precedes advisory-level messages</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>● (Solid circle)</entry>
                  <entry>Active State</entry>
                  <entry>Indicates discrete switch position or active mode</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>○ (Open circle)</entry>
                  <entry>Inactive State</entry>
                  <entry>Indicates discrete switch off or inactive mode</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>⚡ (Lightning bolt)</entry>
                  <entry>Electrical System</entry>
                  <entry>Represents electrical power or electrical system status</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>🔥 (Flame)</entry>
                  <entry>Fire Warning</entry>
                  <entry>Indicates fire detection or overheat condition</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>⛽ (Fuel pump)</entry>
                  <entry>Fuel System</entry>
                  <entry>Represents fuel system components or status</entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
        </specificationContent>
      </specificationSpec>
      <specificationSpec>
        <specificationIdent specificationIdentNumber="HMI-SYM-002"/>
        <specificationTitle>Alert Symbology Hierarchy</specificationTitle>
        <specificationContent>
          <para>Alert symbols shall be displayed in hierarchical order of priority:</para>
          <para>1. Master Warning (RED box with WARNING text) - Highest priority</para>
          <para>2. Master Caution (AMBER box with CAUTION text) - Medium priority</para>
          <para>3. Advisory messages (CYAN diamond) - Lowest priority</para>
          <para>When multiple alerts are active simultaneously, the highest priority alert shall be displayed most prominently with supplementary alerts shown in chronological order.</para>
        </specificationContent>
      </specificationSpec>
      <specificationSpec>
        <specificationIdent specificationIdentNumber="HMI-SYM-003"/>
        <specificationTitle>System Status Icons</specificationTitle>
        <specificationContent>
          <para>Standard icons shall represent aircraft systems on synoptic pages:</para>
          <para>- Hydraulics: Stylized pump and actuator symbols</para>
          <para>- Electrical: Generator, bus, and battery symbols</para>
          <para>- Fuel: Tank, pump, and valve symbols with flow direction arrows</para>
          <para>- Environmental: Pack, valve, and fan symbols with temperature indication</para>
          <para>- Flight Controls: Surface position indicators with control deflection</para>
          <para>- Propulsion: Engine parameters with limit markers and trend indicators</para>
          <para>All synoptic pages shall use consistent symbology and color coding per HMI-COLOR-001 specification.</para>
        </specificationContent>
      </specificationSpec>
      <specificationSpec>
        <specificationIdent specificationIdentNumber="HMI-SYM-004"/>
        <specificationTitle>Text and Font Standards</specificationTitle>
        <specificationContent>
          <para>Text presentation shall follow these guidelines:</para>
          <para>- Font: Sans-serif proportional font optimized for display readability</para>
          <para>- Minimum character height: 3.0 mm for primary information, 2.5 mm for secondary</para>
          <para>- Stroke width to height ratio: 1:6 to 1:8 for optimal legibility</para>
          <para>- Character spacing: Minimum 1 pixel between characters</para>
          <para>- Anti-aliasing: Enabled for all text except at smallest font sizes</para>
          <para>- All-caps usage: Reserved for alerts, warnings, and annunciations</para>
          <para>- Mixed case: Used for normal operational information and labels</para>
        </specificationContent>
      </specificationSpec>
    </specificationRepository>
  </commonRepositoryContent>
</commonRepository>
